{"id":3,"title":"Correlation and Regression","syllabus_module":"Module 3","question":"Which features move with phishing, and can a straight line predict it?","code":[{"label":"Spearman by the rank-difference formula","file":"analysis/03_correlation_regression.R","start_line":22,"code":"rank_difference_rho <- function(x, y) {\n  d <- rank(x) - rank(y)\n  n <- length(x)\n  1 - 6 * sum(d^2) / (n * (n^2 - 1))\n}\npair <- c(\"body_chars\", \"n_words\")\nrho_formula <- rank_difference_rho(train[[pair[1]]], train[[pair[2]]])\nrho_cor <- spearman_mat[pair[1], pair[2]]"},{"label":"Spearman of each feature with is_phish","file":"analysis/03_correlation_regression.R","start_line":33,"code":"# Spearman of each feature with is_phish, phishing vs legitimate only.\npl <- train[train$class %in% c(\"phishing\", \"legitimate\"), ]\npl$is_phish <- as.integer(pl$class == \"phishing\")\nall_features <- c(numeric_features, binary_features)\nrho_phish <- sapply(all_features, function(f) {\n  if (stats::sd(pl[[f]]) == 0) NA_real_ else stats::cor(pl[[f]], pl$is_phish, method = \"spearman\")\n})\nrho_phish <- sort(rho_phish, decreasing = TRUE)"},{"label":"Partial correlation with ppcor","file":"analysis/03_correlation_regression.R","start_line":44,"code":"# Partial correlation: urgency_count vs is_phish given body_chars and n_urls.\ncontrols <- pl[, c(\"body_chars\", \"n_urls\")]\npartial <- rbind(\n  pearson = ppcor::pcor.test(pl$urgency_count, pl$is_phish, controls, method = \"pearson\"),\n  spearman = ppcor::pcor.test(pl$urgency_count, pl$is_phish, controls, method = \"spearman\")\n)\nzero_order <- c(pearson = stats::cor(pl$urgency_count, pl$is_phish),\n                spearman = stats::cor(pl$urgency_count, pl$is_phish, method = \"spearman\"))"},{"label":"Linear probability model and logistic fit","file":"analysis/03_correlation_regression.R","start_line":55,"code":"# Linear probability model and logistic comparison.\npl$log_body_chars <- log(pl$body_chars)\nlpm_formula <- stats::reformulate(c(binary_features, \"log_body_chars\"), response = \"is_phish\")\nlpm <- stats::lm(lpm_formula, data = pl)\nlpm_sum <- summary(lpm)\nlpm_fit <- stats::fitted(lpm)\nout_of_range <- mean(lpm_fit < 0 | lpm_fit > 1)\nlogit <- stats::glm(lpm_formula, data = pl, family = stats::binomial())"}],"console":["The tzdb package is not installed. Timezones will not be available to Arrow compute functions. If you get errors when using Arrow on datetimes, try running `install.packages('tzdb')` and trying again.","Rank-difference rho (body_chars x n_words): formula 0.97155 vs cor() 0.97155 (gap from ties 2.9e-07)","","Spearman with is_phish (phishing vs legitimate, n = 30867 ):","credential_count   has_credential      money_count        has_money ","           0.598            0.567            0.563            0.563 ","generic_greeting     subject_caps    urgency_count      has_urgency ","           0.536            0.402            0.402            0.394 ","      caps_ratio       body_chars          n_words     exclam_count ","           0.292            0.150            0.127            0.025 ","        has_html           ip_url    shortener_url        at_in_url ","           0.016            0.006           -0.002           -0.002 ","         has_url           n_urls ","          -0.071           -0.096 ","","urgency_count vs is_phish: zero-order pearson 0.238 spearman 0.402 ","         estimate p.value statistic     n","pearson     0.371       0      70.3 30867","spearman    0.373       0      70.6 30867","","LPM: R^2 0.5765, multiple R 0.7593, adj R^2 0.5764","             term lpm_estimate     lpm_p logit_estimate logit_odds_ratio","      (Intercept)       0.2375 1.81e-210          0.655            1.925","          has_url      -0.0285  2.65e-30         -0.948            0.388","           ip_url       0.0747  8.56e-02          2.221            9.218","    shortener_url      -0.0523  5.98e-02          0.135            1.145","        at_in_url      -0.0326  1.94e-02     